meta:
  origin:
    producer: World Trade Organization
    title: 'Evolution of trade under the WTO: handy statistics'
    description: |-
      The World Trade Organization (WTO) deals with the global rules of trade between nations. Its main function is to ensure that trade flows as smoothly, predictably and freely as possible.

      This file reports the volume of world trade since 1950, as an annual growth rate and as an index with 1950 = 100. Trade is calculated as the average of exports and imports, and excludes significant re-exports or imports for re-exports.
    citation_full: |-
      World Trade Organization. Evolution of trade under the WTO: handy statistics. Retrieved from https://www.wto.org/english/res_e/statis_e/trade_evolution_e/evolution_trade_wto_e.htm (Accessed: 5 October 2026).
    url_main: https://www.wto.org/english/res_e/statis_e/trade_evolution_e/evolution_trade_wto_e.htm
    url_download: https://www.wto.org/english/res_e/statis_e/trade_evolution_e/world_trade_growth.xlsx
    date_accessed: '2026-10-05'
